 . - udev rule giving the video group access to /dev/dma_heap/system
 Codecs: H.264, HEVC Main/Main10, VP9 Profile 0/2 (no AV1). Chromium
 (xtradeb) decodes H.264/VP9 via V4L2; Firefox and Brave decode H.264/HEVC
 Main (and Main10/VP9 P2 where the firmware exposes P010) via VA-API.
 Needs an erhai kernel with the iris decode-order output property (the 7.2
 line from +b10 on, or any 7.3-rc* line) for Firefox/Brave; the full erhai
 image ships it. The package declares NO Recommends on purpose: the kernel,
 the browsers and libva are provided by the image (or by the user), so
 installing it drags nothing else in. After installing on a running desktop,
 log out and back in once.
